# This repo will be PUBLIC — GitHub Pages' free tier requires it, same trade as ScheduleApp.
# Everything here is either a secret, a local artefact, or a build tool we deliberately don't use.

# ── credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deployment id and secret are entered per device and live in localStorage.
# Nothing of the sort belongs in a repo, least of all a public one.
*creds*
*Creds*
*CREDS*
*secret*
*Secret*
.env
.env.*
.clasprc.json          # clasp's Google credentials, if clasp is ever used
secrets.json

# ── local machine ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── no build toolchain, on purpose ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plain ES modules, zero dependencies. These guards stop a toolchain being
# reintroduced by habit rather than by decision.
*.ts
*.tsx
package.json
package-lock.json
tsconfig*.json
vite.config.*
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# ── project notes, kept out of the public repo ────────────────────────────────
# Requirements, ADRs, the deploy guide and the TODO. Owner's decision: the repo is
# public, and these are not for publication.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
REQUIREMENTS.md
apps-script/README.md

# `apps-script/*.gs` stays tracked — it is source, it holds no secret (SHARED_SECRET is
# a placeholder there), and losing it would mean losing the backend. GitHub Pages does
# not serve it: .github/workflows/pages.yml stages only the app files.
